oolu_016DpBKFMf7ykYSApHtmcFjT", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 64295, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016DpBKFMf7ykYSApHtmcFjT", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 64295, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016DpBKFMf7ykYSApHtmcFjT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 69069, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy in every region, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It has been healthy before, so the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version can safely be repeated, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first request timed out. I retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a second incident or page twice, and the incident list confirms there's only one. The summary covers the cause, the version change and the halted first attempt. It lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the rollout.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01M2qMaFxgLgCfeGDs8qeg2p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", 