ions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out. I'll retry with the same idempotency key, so a repeat can't create a second incident or page twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015TEPWAaadQ9hmTqAQb9pPv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in production in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016DpBKFMf7ykYSApHtmcFjT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy in every region, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It has been healthy before, so the rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version can safely be repeated, so I ran it again and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first request timed out. I retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a second incident or page twice, and the incident list confirms there's only one. The summary covers the cause, the version change and the halted first attempt. It lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the rollout.", "type": "text"}]}]}